IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `New Cardholder (Freedom Card — Miles) Spend & Get Promotion`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENTS. Three, and they do not say the same thing.
--
--   trust-spend-and-get-tnc  Trust Bank Singapore Limited, "New Cardholder
--       (Freedom Card – Miles) Spend & Get Promotion Terms and Conditions",
--       "Last updated on: 21 September 2026, Version: 1". Two pages. The issuer's
--       own terms.
--   trust-freedom-miles-page  the Freedom card Miles product page: a marketing
--       statement, not terms.
--   heymax-trust-welcome-bonus-tnc  HeyMax's article and Terms and Conditions
--       for the Max Miles codes. HeyMax issues and redeems the Max Miles; Trust
--       Bank issues the scratch cards. HeyMax is NOT the issuer of the promotion
--       and its cl.7.2 says "Trust Bank's campaign terms govern card eligibility,
--       Qualified spend and code issuance". Held because the encoding's owner named it.
--
-- WHAT THE ISSUER'S TERMS SAY, and the three things they leave to the
-- cardholder's own "Quest" in the Trust app:
--   Who:    selected Trust customers allocated the Quest during the promotion
--           period, who are (a) a NEW Trust Freedom credit card customer who
--           selected Miles as the initial reward selection, and (b) have no
--           existing or cancelled Trust credit card.
--   Do:     hit the milestones in the Quest "within 31 days of card approval
--           or 30 November 2026 (whichever is earlier)". A digital scratch
--           card arrives "when you meet each specified cumulative Qualifying
--           spend tier (as shown in your Quest)". A transaction must be POSTED
--           (not authorised, pending or unposted) to count.
--   Get:    Max Miles in each scratch card "as indicated in your Quest"
--           (HeyMax's currency). A code from Coupons & Stamps, redeemed once in
--           the HeyMax app; ALL SCRATCH CARDS EXPIRE BY 31 DECEMBER 2026.
-- THE ISSUER'S TERMS FIX NEITHER THE TIERS NOR THE MILES. "Promotion Period:
-- Please refer to your Quest"; "Qualifying spend tier (as shown in your
-- Quest)"; "Max Miles ... as indicated in your Quest".
--
-- WHAT THE PRODUCT PAGE SAYS about the tiers: "20,000 Max Miles when you spend
-- min. S$1,000 OR 50,000 ... S$5,000 OR 100,000 ... S$15,000", "Sign up by 31
-- Oct 2026 to qualify. Spend by 30 Nov 2026 or 31 days after sign-up, whichever
-- is earlier". Three figures joined by OR. It does not say whether they
-- accumulate, replace each other, or are each paid in full.
--
-- WHAT HEYMAX SAYS (cl.3.1, 4.1): Trust Bank issues "a separate unique Max
-- Miles code each time the Participant reaches ... S$1,000 (20,000 Max Miles),
-- a cumulative S$5,000 (a further 30,000 Max Miles), and a cumulative S$15,000
-- (a further 50,000 Max Miles)", "three separate codes totalling 100,000", and
-- the cap "up to 100,000 Max Miles in total". Its article says in terms that
-- "the tiers add up rather than replace each other". It also states the
-- approval window (21 September 2026 0000 SGT to 31 October 2026 2359 SGT),
-- the redemption deadline (31 December 2026 2359 SGT) and the excluded
-- merchant category codes (cl.2.6) and kinds of spend (cl.2.5).
--
-- THE FORK F-trust-tier-additivity (flagged conflict, not a choice). The page's
-- three figures are 20,000, 50,000 and 100,000, which sum to 170,000; HeyMax's
-- three codes are 20,000, 30,000 and 50,000, which sum to 100,000 and are
-- capped at 100,000. They agree on the total of 100,000 only if the page's
-- figures are totals ("OR"). The page does not say so, and the issuer's own
-- terms defer to the Quest. So a purchase that crosses a tier has:
--     floor   = HeyMax's code for that tier (a LUMP when the tier is crossed,
--               20,000 / 30,000 / 50,000), which is also the difference of the
--               page's figures read as totals;
--     ceiling = the page's figure for that tier paid in full (20,000 / 50,000 /
--               100,000) at the crossing. This is the largest the page's words
--               alone could be read to pay at that crossing; it is contradicted
--               by HeyMax cl.4.1 and by HeyMax's own statement of the total.
-- The two agree at the first tier (20,000 either way), so a purchase that
-- crosses only the first tier carries no conflict. Each tier is a lump on
-- crossing and is NOT smoothed into a marginal rate per dollar.
--
-- THE FORK F-trust-sprint-exclusions. HeyMax cl.2.5-2.6 list what does not count
-- as Qualified spend. The issuer's terms say eligible spend is "spend which is
-- not listed as ineligible for cashback rewards under the Trust Freedom credit
-- card and the Trust / NTUC Link credit card product terms": those terms are NOT
-- held, and HeyMax cl.7.2 says Trust's terms govern. So a purchase at a listed
-- code has a floor of 0 (does not count) and a ceiling of counting, and every
-- other answer names that the unheld product terms may exclude the spend.
--
-- THE FORK F-trust-window-basis. The terms say milestones must be hit "within
-- 31 days of card approval or 30 November 2026" and that only posted
-- transactions count. A purchase charged inside the window but posted after it
-- is therefore open: the module counts by POSTING date (the terms' own word)
-- and names the open reading for a purchase charged in and posted after.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Who may earn it`

-- HeyMax cl.2.1: approval "between 21 September 2026, 0000 SGT and 31 October
-- 2026, 2359 SGT". The product page agrees on the end ("Sign up by 31 Oct 2026").
GIVEN approved IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the card approval is inside the offer window` approved MEANS
    approved AT LEAST Date 21 9 2026 AND approved AT MOST Date 31 10 2026

GIVEN h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Trust holder is a new Miles cardholder` h MEANS
    h's `new Trust credit card customer` AND h's `reward choice` EQUALS `Miles`


§§ `When it ends`

-- "within 31 days of card approval or 30 November 2026 (whichever is earlier)".
GIVEN approved IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Trust sprint ends` approved MEANS
    IF approved PLUS 31 AT MOST Date 30 11 2026
    THEN approved PLUS 31
    ELSE Date 30 11 2026

-- "All scratch cards will expire by 31 December 2026."
GIVETH A DATE
`the Trust scratch cards expire` MEANS Date 31 12 2026


§§ `What counts toward a tier`

-- HeyMax cl.2.6: 4900, 6513, 7349; 4829, 5960, 6010, 6011, 6012, 6051, 6211,
-- 6300, 6540; 7995; 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299; 8398, 8651, 8661, 9211,
-- 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405; 7299, 7399, 8999. The same list is held in
-- trust-freedom-miles.l4 for the ongoing earn; each module states its own.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Trust sprint excluded category codes per HeyMax` MEANS
    LIST 4900, 6513, 7349, 4829, 5960, 6010, 6011, 6012, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6540,
         7995, 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299, 8398, 8651, 8661, 9211, 9222,
         9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405, 7299, 7399, 8999

-- Posted, retail, inside the window by posting date, and a new Miles cardholder
-- approved inside the offer window. HeyMax cl.2.5 also excludes cash advances,
-- AXS / SAM / ATM, insurance premiums, instalments, fees and recurring payments
-- and top-ups: those are the kinds `Retail purchase` is not.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase counts toward the Trust sprint` p h MEANS
    `the Trust holder is a new Miles cardholder` h
    AND `the card approval is inside the offer window` (h's `card approved on`)
    AND p's `posting status` EQUALS `Posted to the account`
    AND p's `charge kind` EQUALS `Retail purchase`
    AND NOT (p's `later reversed`)
    AND p's `date posted` AT LEAST (h's `card approved on`)
    AND p's `date posted` AT MOST `the Trust sprint ends` (h's `card approved on`)

-- TRUE iff the purchase was charged inside the window but posted after it: the
-- reading the terms leave open.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is charged in the Trust window and posted after it` p h MEANS
    p's `date charged` AT LEAST (h's `card approved on`)
    AND p's `date charged` AT MOST `the Trust sprint ends` (h's `card approved on`)
    AND p's `date posted` GREATER THAN `the Trust sprint ends` (h's `card approved on`)


§§ `Tiers and Max Miles`

-- HeyMax cl.3.1: the code issued at each tier ("a further" for the second and
-- third): 20,000, then a further 30,000, then a further 50,000.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Max Miles code at each tier per HeyMax` MEANS LIST 20000, 30000, 50000

-- The product page's three figures, joined by "OR", as the page prints them.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Max Miles figure at each tier on the product page` MEANS LIST 20000, 50000, 100000

-- HeyMax cl.4.1: "up to 100,000 Max Miles in total".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Max Miles cap per HeyMax` MEANS 100000

-- The sum of the first n entries of a list.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum of the first` n `of` xs MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER xs
         WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
         WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x PLUS (`the sum of the first` (n MINUS 1) `of` rest)

-- How many of the Quest's cumulative spend tiers a cumulative spend has reached
-- ("one digital scratch card upon completion of each spend tier").
GIVEN tiers IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      spend IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tiers reached by` tiers spend MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN t YIELD t AT MOST spend) tiers)

-- The Max Miles in all the codes issued once n tiers are reached, per HeyMax.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Max Miles after this many tiers per HeyMax` n MEANS
    `the sum of the first` n `of` `the Max Miles code at each tier per HeyMax`

-- The same, if the page's three figures were each paid in full.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Max Miles after this many tiers if the page's figures were each paid` n MEANS
    `the sum of the first` n `of` `the Max Miles figure at each tier on the product page`

GIVEN spend IS A NUMBER
      h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Max Miles unlocked by a cumulative spend of` spend `for` h MEANS
    `the Max Miles after this many tiers per HeyMax` (`the tiers reached by` (h's `Quest spend tiers in S$`) spend)

GIVEN spend IS A NUMBER
      h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Max Miles unlocked on the page's reading by a cumulative spend of` spend `for` h MEANS
    `the Max Miles after this many tiers if the page's figures were each paid` (`the tiers reached by` (h's `Quest spend tiers in S$`) spend)


§§ `The answer for one purchase`

-- The lump this purchase unlocks: the codes for the tiers it crosses, nothing for
-- a purchase that stays inside a tier.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`, m IS A `Trust month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Max Miles this purchase unlocks` p h m MEANS
    IF `the purchase counts toward the Trust sprint` p h
    THEN `the Max Miles unlocked by a cumulative spend of` ((m's `cumulative posted qualifying spend`) PLUS (p's `amount in SGD`)) `for` h
         MINUS `the Max Miles unlocked by a cumulative spend of` (m's `cumulative posted qualifying spend`) `for` h
    ELSE 0

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`, m IS A `Trust month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Max Miles this purchase unlocks on the page's reading` p h m MEANS
    IF `the purchase counts toward the Trust sprint` p h
    THEN `the Max Miles unlocked on the page's reading by a cumulative spend of` ((m's `cumulative posted qualifying spend`) PLUS (p's `amount in SGD`)) `for` h
         MINUS `the Max Miles unlocked on the page's reading by a cumulative spend of` (m's `cumulative posted qualifying spend`) `for` h
    ELSE 0

-- What it unlocks if it posts in the window (the purchase charged in and posted after).
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`, m IS A `Trust month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Max Miles this purchase unlocks if it posts in the window` p h m MEANS
    `the Max Miles unlocked on the page's reading by a cumulative spend of` ((m's `cumulative posted qualifying spend`) PLUS (p's `amount in SGD`)) `for` h
    MINUS `the Max Miles unlocked on the page's reading by a cumulative spend of` (m's `cumulative posted qualifying spend`) `for` h

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`, m IS A `Trust month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`the Trust sprint pays when the spend counts` p h m MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the purchase is charged in the Trust window and posted after it` p h
            THEN `an answer for` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Max Miles` `of` 0 `to` (`the Max Miles this purchase unlocks if it posts in the window` p h m) `wanting` 0 `at` NOTHING `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `Trust Spend and Get` `depending on` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`) `per` "Trust Spend & Get: 'within 31 days of card approval or 30 November 2026'; only posted transactions count"
        IF `the purchase counts toward the Trust sprint` p h
            THEN `an answer for` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Max Miles` `of` (`the Max Miles this purchase unlocks` p h m) `to` (`the Max Miles this purchase unlocks on the page's reading` p h m) `wanting` 0 `at` NOTHING `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `Trust Spend and Get` `depending on` (append (LIST `The issuer's own product terms, which are not held, may exclude this spend`) (IF (`the Max Miles this purchase unlocks` p h m) EQUALS (`the Max Miles this purchase unlocks on the page's reading` p h m) THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)) `per` "Trust Spend & Get: 'Qualifying spend tier (as shown in your Quest)'; HeyMax cl.3.1, 4.1; Freedom Miles page"
        OTHERWISE `nothing is earned on` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Max Miles` `per` "Trust Spend & Get: who may participate; posted transactions in the window"

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`, m IS A `Trust month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`the Trust sprint pays on` p h m MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the code is unknown for` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`nothing is earned on` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Max Miles` `per` "HeyMax cl.2.6: the excluded-MCC list (the code is not known)") `to` (`the Trust sprint pays when the spend counts` p h m) `adding` (LIST `The merchant category code is not known`, `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        IF `the code is among` p `the Trust sprint excluded category codes per HeyMax`
            THEN `bracketed from` (`nothing is earned on` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Max Miles` `per` "HeyMax cl.2.6: the excluded-MCC list") `to` (`the Trust sprint pays when the spend counts` p h m) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        OTHERWISE `the Trust sprint pays when the spend counts` p h m


§§ `The clock the Trust sprint runs on`

-- the terms ("within 31 days of card approval or 30 November 2026"; only posted transactions).
GIVETH A `Period basis`
`the Trust sprint's period` MEANS `A window from card approval`

GIVETH A `Date basis`
`the Trust sprint's date basis` MEANS `Posting date`

#ASSERT `the Trust sprint's period` EQUALS `A window from card approval`
#ASSERT `the Trust sprint's date basis` EQUALS `Posting date`


§§ `Illustrations`

`a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` MEANS `Trust holder` WITH
    `reward choice`                  IS `Miles`
    `new Trust credit card customer` IS TRUE
    `card approved on`               IS Date 22 9 2026
    `Quest spend tiers in S$`        IS LIST 1000, 5000, 15000

`a new Miles cardholder approved on 20 September 2026` MEANS `Trust holder` WITH
    `reward choice`                  IS `Miles`
    `new Trust credit card customer` IS TRUE
    `card approved on`               IS Date 20 9 2026
    `Quest spend tiers in S$`        IS LIST 1000, 5000, 15000

`an existing Trust customer` MEANS `Trust holder` WITH
    `reward choice`                  IS `Miles`
    `new Trust credit card customer` IS FALSE
    `card approved on`               IS Date 22 9 2026
    `Quest spend tiers in S$`        IS LIST 1000, 5000, 15000

`a Cashback cardholder` MEANS `Trust holder` WITH
    `reward choice`                  IS `Cashback`
    `new Trust credit card customer` IS TRUE
    `card approved on`               IS Date 22 9 2026
    `Quest spend tiers in S$`        IS LIST 1000, 5000, 15000

GIVEN spend IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Trust month`
`Trust spend so far` spend MEANS
    `Trust month` WITH `cumulative posted qualifying spend` IS spend

-- The window: "31 days of card approval or 30 November 2026 (whichever is earlier)".
#ASSERT `the Trust sprint ends` (Date 22 9 2026) EQUALS Date 23 10 2026
#ASSERT `the Trust sprint ends` (Date 25 10 2026) EQUALS Date 25 11 2026
#ASSERT `the Trust sprint ends` (Date 30 10 2026) EQUALS Date 30 11 2026
#ASSERT `the Trust sprint ends` (Date 31 10 2026) EQUALS Date 30 11 2026
#ASSERT `the Trust scratch cards expire` EQUALS Date 31 12 2026

-- HeyMax cl.2.1: approval from 21 September to 31 October 2026, inclusive.
#ASSERT NOT (`the card approval is inside the offer window` (Date 20 9 2026))
#ASSERT `the card approval is inside the offer window` (Date 21 9 2026)
#ASSERT `the card approval is inside the offer window` (Date 31 10 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the card approval is inside the offer window` (Date 1 11 2026))

-- Tiers reached: one scratch card per completed tier.
#ASSERT `the tiers reached by` (LIST 1000, 5000, 15000) 999.99 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the tiers reached by` (LIST 1000, 5000, 15000) 1000 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the tiers reached by` (LIST 1000, 5000, 15000) 5000 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the tiers reached by` (LIST 1000, 5000, 15000) 15000 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the tiers reached by` (LIST 1000, 5000, 15000) 40000 EQUALS 3

-- HeyMax cl.3.1: 20,000, a further 30,000, a further 50,000: 100,000 in all, the cap in cl.4.1.
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers per HeyMax` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers per HeyMax` 1 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers per HeyMax` 2 EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers per HeyMax` 3 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers per HeyMax` 3 EQUALS `the Max Miles cap per HeyMax`

-- THE CONFLICT, as numbers. The page's three figures, each paid in full, would be 170,000: more than the 100,000 the same
-- offer is stated to total (HeyMax cl.4.1) and more than HeyMax's own codes. They agree on the first tier and on the page read as totals.
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers if the page's figures were each paid` 1 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers if the page's figures were each paid` 2 EQUALS 70000
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers if the page's figures were each paid` 3 EQUALS 170000
#ASSERT `the Max Miles after this many tiers if the page's figures were each paid` 3 GREATER THAN `the Max Miles cap per HeyMax`

-- A purchase that crosses the first tier unlocks 20,000 whichever reading holds: no conflict named.
-- Posted 10 October 2026 inside the window 22 September to 23 October.
`a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase posted on` `the base purchase` (Date 10 10 2026)) 1100

#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units at best` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT NOT (elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `depends on`))

-- ... one that takes the cumulative spend from S$4,500 to S$5,600 crosses tier 2: HeyMax's further 30,000 is the floor and the
-- page's 50,000 the ceiling, and the conflict is named.
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 4500))'s `units certain` EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 4500))'s `units at best` EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 4500))'s `depends on`)

-- ... one that takes S$14,000 to S$15,100 crosses the third tier: a further 50,000, or the page's 100,000.
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 14000))'s `units certain` EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 14000))'s `units at best` EQUALS 100000

-- ... one purchase that crosses all three tiers at once (S$16,000): the codes for all three, 100,000 by HeyMax and 170,000 on the page's words each paid.
`a Trust purchase of S$16,000 posted 10 October` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase posted on` `the base purchase` (Date 10 10 2026)) 16000
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$16,000 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$16,000 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units at best` EQUALS 170000

-- ... one that stays inside a tier unlocks nothing.
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 1200))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 1200))'s `units at best` EQUALS 0

-- A lump on crossing, not a rate: S$100 more at S$900 crosses the first tier and unlocks 20,000, while S$100 more at S$1,000 unlocks nothing.
`a Trust purchase of S$100 posted 10 October` MEANS `purchase posted on` `the base purchase` (Date 10 10 2026)
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 900))'s `units certain` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 1000))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0

-- Posted after the window closes: it does not count.
`a Trust purchase posted 24 October` MEANS `purchase posted on` (`purchase charged on` `the base purchase` (Date 24 10 2026)) (Date 24 10 2026)
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase posted 24 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s excluded
-- Charged inside the window and posted after it: the open reading.
`a Trust purchase charged 22 October and posted 25 October` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase posted on` (`purchase charged on` `the base purchase` (Date 22 10 2026)) (Date 25 10 2026)) 1100
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase charged 22 October and posted 25 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase charged 22 October and posted 25 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units at best` EQUALS 20000

-- Authorised but not posted does not count.
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` (`purchase with status` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `Authorised but not posted`) `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s excluded

-- Not a new Miles cardholder: an existing customer, or a Cashback choice.
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `an existing Trust customer` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a Cashback cardholder` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s excluded

-- Approved before the offer window opens (HeyMax cl.2.1): does not count.
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `a new Miles cardholder approved on 20 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s excluded

-- A bill payment is not Qualified spend (HeyMax cl.2.5: fees, recurring payments, top-ups, insurance).
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` (`purchase of kind` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` `Bill payment`) `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s excluded

-- F-trust-sprint-exclusions: a listed code has a floor of 0 and a ceiling of counting; an unlisted code (a hospital, 8062) counts.
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` (`recoded purchase` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` 6300) `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` (`recoded purchase` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` 6300) `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units at best` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` (`recoded purchase` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October` 8062) `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT (`the Trust sprint pays on` (`purchase with unknown code` `a Trust purchase of S$1,100 posted 10 October`) `a new Miles cardholder approved on 22 September 2026` (`Trust spend so far` 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT count `the Trust sprint excluded category codes per HeyMax` EQUALS 32
